Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.84,0:00:13.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hughes-san... I'm here again.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.56,0:00:34.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For crying out loud,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.30,0:00:38.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,be more thorough when you rebuild these things, would you, Winry?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.90,0:00:46.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now what do we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.42,0:00:48.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's still a good distance to go \Nbefore we reach Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.86,0:00:50.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.52,0:00:52.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All we can do is walk.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.00,0:00:57.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Eh!? We can't! I might be all right, \Nbut it's going to wear you out, Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.42,0:00:58.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then what would you rather do?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.87,0:01:03.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There aren't any tracks into Ishbal, \Nall the usual roads have been closed down,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.46,0:01:05.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and we can't very well get the military to send us there anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.97,0:01:07.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You {\i1}are{\i0} right about that...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.32,0:01:08.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's just keep going.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.81,0:01:10.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If we just stand around here,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.84,0:01:13.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ishbal isn't very well \Ngoing to come to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.37,0:01:15.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.49,0:01:18.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jeez, why is he always so haphazard?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.89,0:01:23.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.60,0:01:28.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.90,0:01:33.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.63,0:01:39.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.93,0:03:26.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There, you see? \NWe somehow managed to make it!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.90,0:03:30.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Somehow made it? \NWe just arrived at some town, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.98,0:03:35.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In a town this size, we'll be able to \Nprocure a car and anything else we need.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.53,0:03:37.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't! We're kids, after all!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.85,0:03:40.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no way we'll be able to get someone to sell us a car.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.90,0:03:43.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, it's all going to work out.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.32,0:03:46.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, why are you \Nalways like that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.27,0:03:48.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Think ahead a little, would you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.56,0:03:50.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I {\i1}am{\i0} thinking ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.32,0:03:51.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You are not!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.83,0:03:54.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Such as what we're about to do...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.65,0:03:58.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.65,0:04:03.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure \Nit's the right thing to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.69,0:04:08.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I understand how you feel about wanting to stop Scar-san,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.31,0:04:12.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but the goal of our journey is to \Nget our original bodies back, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.98,0:04:13.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well then...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.70,0:04:16.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well then, \Nwhat would you have us do?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.37,0:04:19.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.50,0:04:23.82,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,But maybe we should do something about \Nthe homunculi before dealing with Scar-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.82,0:04:27.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al! Do you even realize what you're saying?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.04,0:04:30.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All I'm saying is that maybe \Nthere are other ways to go about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.94,0:04:32.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know what you mean!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.58,0:04:36.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In any case, I'm saying that you have to think harder about this!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.08,0:04:38.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shut up! \N{\i1}You{\i0} think harder about it!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.75,0:04:43.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-What are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.67,0:04:46.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ha! That's what you get for talking too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.28,0:04:47.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're awful!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.68,0:04:49.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If that's how you want it, \NI'll show you!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.85,0:04:56.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, {\i1}you're{\i0} the one \Nwho needs to cool his head!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.82,0:04:58.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now you've done it!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.13,0:05:03.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Take that!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.28,0:05:05.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jeez, what are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.58,0:05:08.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dammit!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.65,0:05:10.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.19,0:05:13.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you little...!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.18,0:05:29.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, why are you always like that?! Why are you so stubborn?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.89,0:05:31.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not stubborn!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.54,0:05:32.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, you are!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.90,0:05:34.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, if you'd act \Nmore accommodating,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.63,0:05:36.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,maybe we could discuss this with Dad or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.26,0:05:37.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't be ridiculous!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.13,0:05:39.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter what happens, I'll never ask for his help!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.56,0:05:41.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's you being stubborn!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.57,0:05:43.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sh-Shut up!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.33,0:05:46.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Suit yourself!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.78,0:05:48.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.35,0:05:51.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, I say!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.30,0:05:54.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I haven't seen you in a while, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.75,0:05:59.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, Book... Book-bull... I mean, Bookworm-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.03,0:06:01.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's Scieszka.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.86,0:06:03.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.13,0:06:04.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, Winwin-san...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.84,0:06:06.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's Winry.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.43,0:06:07.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.94,0:06:10.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.69,0:06:12.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes? What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.71,0:06:14.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, you go first.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.47,0:06:17.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh, well...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.23,0:06:21.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The truth is, there's something I'd like to discuss with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.67,0:06:22.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With me?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.45,0:06:29.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've been investigating for a long time \Nabout why Lt. Colonel—
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.55,0:06:33.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I mean, why Brigadier General Hughes had to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.45,0:06:37.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel—I mean, \NBrigadier General Hughes—
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.25,0:06:38.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Er...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.79,0:06:40.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why don't we just \Ncall him Hughes-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.39,0:06:43.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.38,0:06:44.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.73,0:06:47.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's strange.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.47,0:06:48.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Strange?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.50,0:06:54.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The more I look into it, the more strange things keep turning up.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.01,0:06:57.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know what \NI should do about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.15,0:06:59.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are you telling me this?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.65,0:07:02.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't trust anyone in the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.38,0:07:04.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not even Colonel Mustang.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.57,0:07:08.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please! I can't take this anymore!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.57,0:07:11.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I don't tell someone, I'll... I'll...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.73,0:07:13.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right! All right, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.99,0:07:14.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Calm down.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.53,0:07:17.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.00,0:07:23.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sheesh, what's his deal?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.01,0:07:26.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You gotta be kidding me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.23,0:07:28.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, pass the salt.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.02,0:07:36.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Damn...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.53,0:07:46.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These are the materials that Hughes-san had me bring together and copy down.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.89,0:07:51.40,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,And these are the materials I used to \Nreference them, which I've collected on my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.39,0:07:56.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh, you're not saying you \Nwant me to read {\i1}all{\i0} of this, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.41,0:07:57.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.47,0:07:58.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's absolutely impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.82,0:08:00.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How many months do you think that would take?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.57,0:08:04.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that right? \NIn that case, allow me...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.63,0:08:08.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It started with the accident that collapsed the 5th Laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.41,0:08:13.47,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,There aren't any records, so there's no way for me \Nto know what was happening in the shadows.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.73,0:08:17.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, that's where \NHughes-san's investigation began.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.19,0:08:18.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.95,0:08:22.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes? What did you find out?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.90,0:08:28.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right. Hughes-san was investigating the 5th Laboratory and the Ishbalan Rebellion.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.57,0:08:29.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ishbal?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.96,0:08:32.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is just my conjecture, but I think
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.68,0:08:37.07,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,that Hughes-san discovered an important secret that he wasn't supposed to know, and...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.22,0:08:39.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was killed?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.99,0:08:44.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, okay! I get it! Don't cry!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.62,0:08:51.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, you dummy...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.29,0:08:56.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al! Do you even realize what you're saying?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.28,0:08:58.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, I do!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.12,0:09:00.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know at least that \N{\i1}she{\i0} is ahead of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.89,0:09:11.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother?! Jeez, where were—
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.54,0:09:14.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.02,0:09:15.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Long time no see.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.63,0:09:20.64,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,As I was looking through this material, \NI kept running into a certain person's name.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.64,0:09:21.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What person?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.21,0:09:23.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Captain Juliet Douglas,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.88,0:09:27.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the woman they say was the trigger for the Ishbalan Rebellion.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.94,0:09:29.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But something is strange about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.43,0:09:34.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She died in an accident two years before the Ishbalan Rebellion.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.76,0:09:37.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can I have you look at this?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.34,0:09:42.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.87,0:09:45.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was in Hughes-san's files.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.99,0:09:48.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He sent away to \Nher hometown for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.98,0:09:52.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The year she died is two years \Nbefore the Ishbalan Rebellion, all right,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.76,0:09:54.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but it's just some \Nkind of error, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.44,0:09:57.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Some mistake in the records, or someone with the same name or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.55,0:10:01.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are no mistakes in the government records, or in the military records.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.27,0:10:02.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's more...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.70,0:10:03.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's more?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.82,0:10:07.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's still in the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.03,0:10:10.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please look at this.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.22,0:10:13.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's going on here?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.07,0:10:19.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,According to the grave record, she died two years before the Ishbalan Rebellion.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.07,0:10:20.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, according to the military materials,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.67,0:10:24.27,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,she fought in the war against Ishbal, without her name being cleared from the enlistment rolls,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.27,0:10:28.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and currently, she has been \Npromoted to the Führer's secretary.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.75,0:10:30.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's strange, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.13,0:10:33.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone who's supposed to be dead \Nis the Führer's secretary?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.78,0:10:35.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not all, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.64,0:10:37.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's more?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.03,0:10:39.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If she really is alive,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.61,0:10:41.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then at the very least, \Nshe has to be in her fifties.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.87,0:10:45.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But right now, the Juliet-san that is serving as the Führer's secretary
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.49,0:10:49.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,has to be in her mid-thirties any way you look at it!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.75,0:10:52.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She died, but she's not dead! She doesn't age, either!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.71,0:10:54.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who in the world \Nis this woman?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.24,0:10:59.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,These are all things that I could not explain,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.17,0:11:01.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but after I became desperate and thought about it all,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.51,0:11:03.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I arrived at a certain hypothesis.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.66,0:11:06.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A hypothesis?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.95,0:11:11.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If my hypothesis is right, then all of the inconsistencies are swept away.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.74,0:11:17.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Juliet Douglas-san...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.61,0:11:23.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is an alien.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.66,0:11:28.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, I don't think so. \NNot a chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.01,0:11:29.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then what else could it be?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.02,0:11:32.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.25,0:11:36.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But if we continue \Nto investigate this,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.05,0:11:39.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we'll find out who killed Hughes-san, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.48,0:11:41.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But how do we do that?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.22,0:11:46.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am a soldier for the time being, but I'm a records clerk,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.23,0:11:48.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and with Juliet-san \Nbeing with the Führer,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.90,0:11:51.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't very well \Nget too close to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.20,0:11:54.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't investigate \Nwhat she's up to.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.34,0:11:59.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, what if we were to wiretap her line, to find out more about her?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.85,0:12:03.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wiretap?! That's the thing that wives do \Nto get evidence on their husbands
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.30,0:12:05.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,when they're going \Nthrough a divorce, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.81,0:12:07.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know if I can do that...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.84,0:12:09.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure you can!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.79,0:12:12.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's wiretap!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.31,0:12:17.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel-san, \Nwhat are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.80,0:12:19.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I followed you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.03,0:12:22.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wanted you to tell me about your enemies.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.46,0:12:23.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My enemies?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.06,0:12:26.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those guys who dress all in black.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.40,0:12:29.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you going to do to them once you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.55,0:12:30.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's obvious.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.20,0:12:32.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Take my revenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.50,0:12:41.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry about my uniform.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.90,0:12:46.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When all you do is heavy labor, \Nyour arms do tend to thicken up, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.10,0:12:48.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe I should go on \Na diet or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.58,0:12:52.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As far as that matter goes, I'll make out the report.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.80,0:13:06.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is something the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.52,0:13:08.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.48,0:13:14.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you know those \Ntwo people from earlier?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.33,0:13:16.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, from before.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.74,0:13:20.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is it. The telephone lines should all be concentrated in this facility.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.69,0:13:25.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But there are \Nso many locks on it,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.51,0:13:28.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and there must be some \Nsecure alarm devices, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.55,0:13:30.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It won't be all that easy \Nto slip in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.94,0:13:32.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's open.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.78,0:13:35.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This much was easy, easy!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.95,0:13:37.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A-Amazing...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.62,0:13:39.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.40,0:13:45.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, where is her room?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.86,0:13:48.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The central hall, number 103.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.89,0:13:51.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,103... 103...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.63,0:13:52.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.39,0:13:55.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right, we're okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.74,0:13:57.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now we just have to wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.78,0:14:03.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're wrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.29,0:14:05.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you do this, then it won't mean anything for Greed-san, Roa-san and the others
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.61,0:14:07.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to have protected you, Martel-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.86,0:14:10.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know about me, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.71,0:14:16.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm a Chimera. I can't go on living as a regular person anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.24,0:14:18.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've lost my friends, Greed-san,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.48,0:14:21.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and the only place \Nwhere I could have lived.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.21,0:14:23.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you can't take revenge \Nbecause of it!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.37,0:14:24.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It won't do any good \Nto try to stop me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.89,0:14:28.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm half snake now, \Nso my vindictiveness runs deep.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.72,0:14:31.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You just can't do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.59,0:14:35.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She reminds me of Scar-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.80,0:14:39.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There isn't anything left for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.57,0:14:42.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And those guys are \Nyour enemies, aren't they?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.71,0:14:44.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, \NI'll take care of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.30,0:14:49.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't plan on assisting you \Nin your revenge,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.35,0:14:50.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,nor do I intend \Nto let you take it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.24,0:14:52.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why not?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.14,0:14:55.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because I'm sure that's what \NRoa-san and the others were thinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.81,0:14:57.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,See you around.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.69,0:15:06.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's right. That's why I have to stop them—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.26,0:15:08.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}both Scar-san and Martel-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.51,0:15:14.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.22,0:15:19.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's no easy task finding him.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.86,0:15:34.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward! Hey, Edward!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.99,0:15:38.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't find Alphonse anywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.60,0:15:40.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did something happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.08,0:15:42.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How should I know about him?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.23,0:15:44.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fighting again?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.54,0:15:46.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's his fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.48,0:15:50.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He keeps pestering me about when Dad is coming home.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.32,0:15:54.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is a problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.55,0:15:56.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder where \NAlphonse could have gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.87,0:16:00.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just don't know \Nwhere he could be.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.44,0:16:07.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why do I have to go?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.30,0:16:25.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.22,0:16:47.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, Führer's Office.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.23,0:16:51.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...communication coming in \Non a public line. Their code is...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.21,0:16:53.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,zero, eigh... two.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.67,0:16:55.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please put it through.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.49,0:16:57.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here it comes! Here it comes!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.46,0:17:01.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, it's me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.14,0:17:02.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Envy,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.42,0:17:05.92,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,using regular phone lines is supposed to be forbidden except in cases of emergency.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.92,0:17:07.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't be so strict.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.89,0:17:10.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're the one who said to report in, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.73,0:17:12.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm almost there, in the north.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.67,0:17:14.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's so quiet here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.21,0:17:16.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If things stay this calm, then I might have to—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.51,0:17:19.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You will faithfully \Ncarry out your task.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.04,0:17:22.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is this? Envy?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.83,0:17:26.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Envy is one of those homunculi that Ed was talking about.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.66,0:17:31.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm hanging up. It sounds like \NI've got one more job to take care of.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.57,0:17:43.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why don't we get \Nout of here now?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.20,0:17:44.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.63,0:17:48.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, about that \Nconversation just now...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.11,0:17:51.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What in the world \Nwere they talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.60,0:17:53.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who knows? But somehow,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.96,0:17:56.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it seemed like they were talking about something dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.86,0:18:01.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It looks like it's going to take \Na lot more time to gather any evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.87,0:18:07.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even by trying wiretapping and such, it's not going to be all that easy, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.60,0:18:09.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.50,0:18:21.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's get out of here!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.92,0:18:24.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.91,0:18:25.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.92,0:18:30.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is that thing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.70,0:18:32.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How should I know?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.01,0:18:39.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh, what's the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.37,0:18:41.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That girl! That girl!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.56,0:18:52.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The exit!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.33,0:18:57.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.18,0:19:15.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Their mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.34,0:19:19.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed and Al's...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.30,0:19:20.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.13,0:19:25.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry-chan?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.64,0:19:30.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So it {\i1}was{\i0} you, Winry-chan!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.14,0:19:32.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you doing \Nin a place like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.62,0:19:38.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're saved!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.40,0:19:41.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's an alien, all right!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.11,0:19:42.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,An alien?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.44,0:20:04.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.04,0:20:09.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.70,0:20:12.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going to Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.68,0:20:16.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's stop Scar-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.45,0:20:28.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How did you know \NI would be there?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.92,0:20:30.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You haven't changed.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.91,0:20:34.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You always used to sulk down by the riverside
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.11,0:20:36.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,whenever we got into \Na fight, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.66,0:20:38.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I guess so.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.59,0:20:44.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do we do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.85,0:20:48.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not much we can do \Nexcept walk.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.23,0:20:53.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Want to hop on?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.39,0:20:55.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Martel-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.00,0:20:57.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, you know her?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.76,0:20:58.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.75,0:21:02.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, we'll take you up on that \Nif you'd be so kind.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.98,0:21:04.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,H-Hold on, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.77,0:21:05.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where's the harm?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.95,0:21:08.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've got to help each other out when we're in trouble, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.08,0:21:19.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to \Nmake sure I stop you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.68,0:21:24.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right then, we're off!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.28,0:21:25.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.55,0:21:34.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Something wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.38,0:21:36.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mm-mm.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.33,0:21:39.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, do you remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.99,0:21:42.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The first time we ever \Ngot into a fight?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.82,0:21:46.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, you mean the time \Nyou tossed me around, Al.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.20,0:21:48.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was the first time I ever went down to the riverside.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.99,0:21:50.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.24,0:21:51.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.28,0:21:55.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When we were at Sensei's place, \Nyou'd disappear right after we'd fight, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.84,0:21:58.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks to you, I had to work for both of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.04,0:22:02.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We even fought over which one of us \Nwas going to marry Winry, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.12,0:22:03.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We argued about that?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.79,0:22:05.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We did!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.28,0:23:39.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.93,0:23:42.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 39: "Eastern Civil War"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.94,0:23:48.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The place that Scar has chosen \Nis a city that we will never forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.23,0:23:50.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The name of that city is Liore.
